# Backend file placement

`server/` is already too flat. New modules go in a domain folder. Do not add new `server/fooOps.js` files at the root.

| Kind | Put it here |
|------|-------------|
| HTTP route registration | `server/http/` (composer stays `server/httpApi.js` until split) |
| Auth / sessions / RBAC | `server/auth/` (existing `auth.js` stays until a dedicated move) |
| Sales, customers, quotations, refunds | `server/sales/` |
| Finance, GL, treasury, accounting | `server/finance/` |
| HR | `server/hr/` (existing `hr*.js` stay until a dedicated move) |
| Procurement / suppliers / POs | `server/procurement/` |
| Production / coils / inventory | `server/operations/` |
| Office / work items / filing | `server/office/` |
| Workspace search / rooms / inbox | `server/workspace/` |
| Isomorphic domain math | `shared/lib/` (frontend copies via sync script) |

When moving a file: `git mv`, update imports, keep tests beside the module (`*.test.js`). Prefer a thin re-export at the old path only if many test/e2e imports would break in the same PR.

Do not move files that already have unrelated uncommitted edits. Do not split `httpApi.js` / `writeOps.js` / `readModel.js` without keeping tests green.
